From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:54:56 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 60/76] flashnext cuda: a pipeline stage runs its verify
 windows as graphs

A stage's drafted windows ran eagerly: the window graph was off whenever
the engine had a hop. Each stage now captures its own layers with its
boundary rows' send and receive, as --tp 2 captures its collectives:
the nonblocking communicator waits on the host only, outside the graph.
A pass that must settle a late prompt chunk's rows stays eager, and only
the embedding stage gathers n-gram rows before a window.

flashnext-span checks it on one GPU: after the two stages' prompt, each
runs its windows on its own thread and stream, the rows crossing device
flags a graph captures, and every window row's scores must equal the
eager engine's; a planted control spoils rank 1's first rows.
